  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1...Isolated to scattered snow/rain showers will \noccur through today.\n\nKEY MESSAGE 1 DESCRIPTION...\nAn upper level disturbance moves south across the region \ntoday, which will support isolated to scattered snow/rain \nshowers. Any snow accumulations today through will be minimal, \ngenerally only a few tenths of an inch. However, local \naccumulations up to around an inch could occur across higher \nterrain areas.\n\nKEY MESSAGE 2...Persistent dry conditions the rest of this week\nwill lead to a worsening of the ongoing water resource drought \nimpacting Eastern and Northern Maine.\n\nKEY MESSAGE 2 DESCRIPTION...\nA large high pressure system centered over the Mid-Atlantic \ncoast will remain fairly stationary throughout next week. Upper \nair models indicate a very slow moving ridge that keeps high \npressure in place. Warm, dry air from the desert SW is expected \nto be piped into the region, which should bring temps into the \nlow 50s Wednesday through Friday. Possible breezy conditions \nduring the day will further lead to dry conditions. This \ncontinued dry weather will allow for soil moisture to dry/remain\nat much below normal levels next week.",
